				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Mist): Replace em-dashes with hyphens in README.md\n\nStandardise all em-dash (—) typographic characters to regular hyphens (-) across the README for consistency with the project's plain-text formatting conventions. Em-dashes in markdown source can cause inconsistent rendering across editors and diff tools.\n\nAffects bullet lists, definition lists, the Related Documentation section, and inline descriptions throughout the file. No content changes.",
			"SHA": "9d625d1158709eb72756f1548cf4cfafe00e814f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T20:04:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "style(Mist): Reflow markdown text and standardise table formatting in README and DeepDive\n\nReflow prose paragraphs in both README.md and Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md to stay within the project line-width convention, preventing hard-wrap inconsistencies that cause noisy diffs on subsequent edits.\n\nStandardise all markdown tables across both files: add alignment dashes, normalise column widths, and apply consistent spacing between pipe delimiters. Fix the Related Documentation indentation in README.md from tabs to standard two-space continuation.\n\nNo content changes — formatting and whitespace only.",
			"SHA": "4c83435bd9b5e634367fa7776ae40a970d2354f9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "style(Mist): Format code and doc-comment whitespace across four sources\n\nNormalise inconsistent whitespace in Source files: fix tab-indented code in Library.rs doc examples (tabs→spaces), reflow wide doc-comment lines in Resolver.rs and Zone.rs to stay under the project line-width convention, remove a trailing blank line in WebSocket's ServeLocal telemetry call, break long chained closures in AuthorizeUpgrade and ConnectWithSecret across multiple lines, and add vertical spacing between parameters in AuthorizeUpgrade's signature.\n\nNo functional changes — formatting and whitespace only.",
			"SHA": "44086a7ecf1be9afbdc1a976557e1819a26c03b2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:48:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Normalise doc-comment sections and add missing module-level docs\n\nStandardise doc-comment formatting across all six public source files. The\nprimary change is upgrading section headings from single-hash to double-hash\n(`# Parameters` → `## Parameters`, `# Returns` → `## Returns`, `# Example` →\n`## Example`) so they nest correctly under the outer item-level doc comment\ndelimiter.\n\nAdd module-level doc comments with `## Functions` or `## Types` listings to\nResolver.rs, Server.rs, and Zone.rs, matching the pattern already established\nin the crate's earlier source files. Add missing `## Parameters` and `## Returns`\nsections to `LandResolver`, `LandDnsResolver::New`, `LandDnsResolver::new`,\n`SharedSecret::random`, `SharedSecret::as_hex`, and `reqwest::dns::Resolve::resolve`.\nAdd `## Errors` sections to `Serve` and `ServeSync` documenting the failure\nconditions (non-loopback bind, hickory runtime errors).\n\nFix indentation in doc-example code blocks in Library.rs (tabs to spaces) and\nmark a TODO-style note in ForwardSecurity.rs with the currently authorised\nallowlist domain (`update.editor.land`).\n\nNo functional changes — documentation and formatting only.",
			"SHA": "edb464753eaad464a74c0bb13cdf37fbb9d3c24f"
